{"title":"2007 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Alternative_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Alternative Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the center of the circle circumscribed about triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/6/336358a364ce49b354744d52dd99f5b0b69a48b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BOC = 120^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b58a8ef08202a51a05a99afd914c57fe7a1937.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOB = 140^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"113\" height=\"13\" />, as shown. What is the degree measure of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/a/a3ad57710b6810476e6017ea2c2cc6d41219c218.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2007_12B_AMC-3.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/8/8a/2007_12B_AMC-3.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"292\" height=\"297\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/a/30abbe541457f5cf23163efa890a9ef10a527309.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm {(A)} 35 \\qquad \\mathrm {(B)} 40 \\qquad \\mathrm {(C)} 45 \\qquad \\mathrm {(D)} 50 \\qquad  \\mathrm {(E)} 60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"359\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/0/890bd5d40a42153edcb992ad0a14cac52ca2eaf8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABO$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d9b534de592b2a7fc63b97e1f0faab799204e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOC$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> are isosceles, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/e/84edf39f2b0f30efa403bd0237fe917372fa4326.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABO=20^o$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/9/de976d018105538a8152aadf5894f15e36f9f0ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OBC=30^o$\" width=\"105\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e1484f37b5fc4f5d56ad36d9b2c4c8758a51f7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABC=50^o$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/b/bfbf4df7c25681bb178ddc50ee0c0d656aa25b5e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"26\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Alternative_Solution\">Alternative Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Alternative Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/9/b49f118cc2dd006ea986ea62cff5e5fe87679e1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle AOC = 100^{\\circ} \\implies \\angle ABC =\\frac{\\angle AOC}{2} =50^{ \\circ},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"360\" height=\"39\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/7/ef723f3ebbeebb8f248c9ec4526c803a0ebe7bc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(D)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2007_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody>